  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Identify Quadratic Function from Graph</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The graph of a quadratic function \(f(x)\) is shown below:</p>
<p>{@plot(f_x, [x, xmin, xmax], [y, -10, 10])@}</p>
<p>The vertex of the parabola is at \(({@vx@}, {@vy@})\), and the curve passes through the point \(({@px@}, {@py@})\).</p>
<p>Find the algebraic formula for \(f(x)\):</p>
<p>\(f(x) =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The vertex of the parabola is \((h, k) = ({@vx@}, {@vy@})\). In vertex form:</p>
\[ f(x) = a(x - {@vx@})^2 + {@vy@} \]
<p>Substitute the point \(({@px@}, {@py@})\) to determine \(a\):</p>
\[ {@py@} = a({@px@} - {@vx@})^2 + {@vy@} \]
\[ {@py@} = a(1)^2 + {@vy@} \implies a = {@a@} \]
<p>Hence the formula is:</p>
\[ f(x) = {@f_x@} \]]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1000000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber>demo-quadratic-graph</idnumber>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2025102100</text>
    </stackversion>
    <questionvariables>
      <text><![CDATA[/* Quadratic in vertex form: f(x) = a*(x - h)^2 + k */
a: rand([2, -2, 3]);
h: rand([-3, -2, -1, 1, 2, 3]);
k: rand([-4, -3, -2, 2, 3, 4]);

f_x: a*(x - h)^2 + k;
ta1: f_x;

/* Misconception expressions */
ans_no_a: (x - h)^2 + k;
ans_sign_flip: a*(x + h)^2 + k;

/* Key coordinates */
vx: h;
vy: k;
px: h + 1;
py: ev(f_x, x = px);

xmin: h - 4;
xmax: h + 4;
]]></text>
    </questionvariables>
